Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{
 "research_concepts": ["structural roles", "influence", "cut-heavy shapers", "drive-heavy shapers", "role portability across contexts", "play-type possession records derived from play-by-play", "shot creation and off-ball cutting"],
 "methodological_questions": ["Can role portability be tested with n=24 units?", "How should portability be measured across seasons or regular season versus playoffs?", "What sample size and power are needed to compare two play-style groups?", "How reliable are play-type labels derived from play-by-play?", "Are usage, minutes, and lineup context confounding the cut-versus-drive contrast?"],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-057",
   "status_as_recorded": "supported",
   "finding": "In 92 connector movers, pre-move cut share predicted whether connector function reproduced after a move (rho +0.265, LOO AUC 0.622, permutation p=0.005; holds when dropping Gafford). The record calls this exploratory, notes that almost all other pre-move predictors were null, and says the paper treats cut share as a boundary condition. Its sample is connector movers defined by organizational function, not NBA play-type shapers in the 2022-23 to 2025-26 data."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-090",
   "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
   "finding": "Tested whether matching a mover's initiation diet to a destination's thin jobs predicts post-move outcomes. Of 198 movers, 19 were taxonomy connectors and the 15.7% match rate left 5 matched connectors. The all-movers binary result (p=0.0283) did not hold as a continuous Spearman (-0.034). Connector-specific delta match was +0.540 vs +0.069 (p=0.156, n=5/14). Recorded verdict: null."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-024",
   "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
   "finding": "Tested DRIVE-as-BEST counters against a feasibility-constrained play-type mix on 44 triggers from 13 teams. Observed gap was -0.066 (p=0.2175 vs B_fixed). Minimum detectable effect at 80% power was about 0.180 PPP (SD about 0.34), so a null and an effect up to 0.18 PPP could not be distinguished."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-029",
   "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
   "finding": "Archived check of whether mover portability relates to destination net-rating change. Recorded as 'underpowered and null once corrected for landing-spot quality'. No numbers were kept, and it was dropped from Paper 1. Its failure type is recorded as A_unanswerable."
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-090",
   "what_failed": "Binary diet-to-destination match on connector subsets, with an all-movers binary test and a continuous Spearman follow-up.",
   "why": "Recorded as LIM:small_sample. Only 19 taxonomy connectors and 5 matched connectors remained after matching. The all-movers binary result did not replicate as a continuous Spearman, so the connector-specific test was not licensed."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-024",
   "what_failed": "Counter-effect test of DRIVE-as-BEST triggers against a constrained play-type mix.",
   "why": "Recorded as LIM:low_power_large_MDE and LIM:small_sample. With n=44 the observed gap was below the MDE of 0.180 PPP, so the null is uninformative."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-PAP-029",
   "what_failed": "Mover portability versus destination net-rating change.",
   "why": "Recorded as LIM:low_power_large_MDE and LIM:small_sample, stated as underpowered and requiring a landing-spot correction. No numbers were kept, so the result cannot be checked."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "Earlier project work has tested cut-versus-drive and play-type portability questions only on small or differently defined samples: 92 connector movers in FAM:SF-CHT-057, 19 taxonomy connectors in FAM:SF-APPS-090, 44 triggers in FAM:SF-APPS-024, and an unreported archive check in FAM:SF-PAP-029.",
  "Small-sample comparisons of this kind have repeatedly been underpowered or unlicensed. FAM:SF-APPS-024 and FAM:SF-PAP-029 record low power, and FAM:SF-APPS-090 records a binary result that did not survive a continuous test.",
  "FAM:SF-CHT-057 is the only retrieved record with a positive cut-share portability signal. It is exploratory, its sample is connector movers rather than the 24 shaper units, and it reports cut share as a boundary condition rather than a general effect."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "No retrieved record tests cut-heavy versus drive-heavy NBA shapers using 2022-23 to 2025-26 play-by-play-derived possession records.",
  "No retrieved record shows that cut share predicts role portability for shapers. FAM:SF-CHT-057 is about connectors moving between organizations, and the cut-share result may not transfer to shaper roles or to within-team or playoff contexts.",
  "No retrieved record gives a usable power calculation for n=24 units. FAM:SF-PAP-029 kept no numbers, and FAM:SF-APPS-024 gives an MDE for n=44 only.",
  "The retrieved records do not show whether portability is defined as reproduction across seasons, teams, or regular season versus playoffs, so the outcome definition cannot be checked against them."
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "With n=24 split into two groups of about 12, a two-sample comparison at alpha 0.05 and 80% power can only detect a very large standardized difference (roughly d of 1.2 or more). This is my calculation, not a retrieved result.",
  "A cut-versus-drive contrast on 24 units is likely to be confounded by usage, minutes, position, and team context, and possibly by the play-type label itself, since portability may be measured with the same possession data that defines cut and drive shares.",
  "If the question is kept, a defensible test needs more units, such as player-season or player-context observations, than the 24 recorded units. Otherwise the result would be descriptive."
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "The unit count of 24 is recorded as 'units available to a study of this question' and may not be the same as player-seasons, so the true sample for a shaper-level test is not known.",
  "Portability has no defined operational outcome in the task statement. Candidates include reproduction of cut or drive share across seasons, team changes, or regular season versus playoffs, and each would need a separate definition.",
