  "FAM:SF-CHT-057 has a status of supported, but the record calls it exploratory and reports p=0.011 in one place and a permutation p=0.005 in another. Its sample and definition differ from the present question.",
  "The archived record FAM:SF-PAP-029 has no numbers, so its effect size cannot be used."
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes",
  "explanation": "The retrieved records show that comparable small-sample tests in this project were underpowered, unlicensed, or untestable (FAM:SF-APPS-024, FAM:SF-APPS-090, FAM:SF-PAP-029). Together with the exploratory, differently defined FAM:SF-CHT-057 signal, this moved the decision from a provisional proceed toward do_not_proceed as a confirmatory test on 24 units. The historical evidence does not show the question is unanswerable in principle, so the recommended path is a descriptive analysis or a redesigned study with more units."
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": 0.15,
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {"code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER", "text": "With 24 units, only very large group differences are detectable. FAM:SF-APPS-024 and FAM:SF-PAP-029 record the same low-power problem in comparable settings."},
   {"code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY", "text": "Cut and drive shares come from derived play-type labels, and their reliability and portability measure are not established in the retrieved records."},
   {"code": "CONFOUNDING", "text": "Usage, minutes, position, lineup, and team context may drive both play style and any observed portability, and the 24-unit sample cannot adjust for them adequately."}
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "partly",
  "cited": ["FAM:SF-CHT-057", "FAM:SF-APPS-090", "FAM:SF-APPS-024", "FAM:SF-PAP-029"],
  "summary": "Earlier project work has examined related questions on connector movers and drive-versus-cut play types. FAM:SF-CHT-057 reports a supported but exploratory cut-share effect in 92 connector movers, with the paper treating it as a boundary condition. FAM:SF-APPS-090, FAM:SF-APPS-024, and FAM:SF-PAP-029 are untestable or underpowered in small samples. None of these tests cut-heavy versus drive-heavy NBA shapers in the 2022-23 to 2025-26 data with 24 units, so the question is only partly answered by prior work and is not answered for this sample."
 },
 "risks": [
  {"code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER", "text": "n=24 gives very low power for a two-group comparison, and a null would be uninformative about moderate effects."},
  {"code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY", "text": "Cut-heavy and drive-heavy classifications depend on derived play-type labels whose reliability is unknown."},
  {"code": "OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL", "text": "If portability is defined from the same possession-level play-type data, the outcome and the predictor may share a label, which inflates apparent portability."},
  {"code": "CONFOUNDING", "text": "Usage, minutes, role on team, and lineup context may account for both play style and portability differences."},
  {"code": "DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY", "text": "Seasons from 2022-23 to 2025-26 and regular season versus playoffs may differ in play style and role transfer, so pooled portability estimates may mix contexts."},
  {"code": "MULTIPLE_TESTING", "text": "Choosing among several portability definitions, play-type cutoffs, and subgroups would inflate false positives unless the primary contrast is fixed in advance."},
  {"code": "LABEL_ERROR", "text": "Possession attribution and initiator assignment from play-by-play may misclassify cut and drive possessions."}
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": 0.07,
  "rejected": 0.05,
  "untestable": 0.5,
  "artifact": 0.03,
  "uncertain": 0.35
 },
 "decision": "do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "Difference in portability between cut-heavy and drive-heavy shapers, where portability is a pre-specified measure of how far a shaper's role reproduces across a context change (for example, regular season to playoffs or season to season). The question as posed does not define the outcome, so this estimand must be fixed before any run.",
  "unit": "Player-season (or player-context) shaper observation, not the team or the 24 recorded units unless those are confirmed to be shaper-level.",
  "sample": "The 24 units as recorded from NBA 2022-23 to 2025-26 regular seasons and playoffs, used only for a descriptive pilot. A confirmatory test would need more units, and the minimum sample must be set from a power calculation before data are read.",
  "power": "At n=24 (about 12 per group) only a very large standardized difference (d of about 1.2 or more) is detectable at alpha 0.05 and 80% power (own calculation). Any confirmatory claim requires a pre-registered MDE and a sample that reaches it; otherwise the result is reported as descriptive.",
  "controls": "Adjust for minutes, usage rate, position, team and lineup context, and season. Use a derived-label reliability check (for example, split-half or inter-coder agreement on a sample of possessions) before classifying shapers as cut-heavy or drive-heavy. Do not use the outcome to define the labels.",
  "falsification": "Permutation test of cut-share labels against the portability outcome (as in FAM:SF-CHT-057), plus a placebo contrast using a non-play-style trait. Expect the placebo to be null; a non-null placebo signals confounding or label leakage.",
  "multiplicity": "One pre-specified primary contrast (cut-heavy minus drive-heavy portability under one fixed definition). All other definitions, subgroups, and cutoffs are secondary and corrected with Holm, or reported as exploratory.",
  "decision_rule": "Claim support only if the primary contrast is significant at the pre-specified alpha after the fixed controls, the effect exceeds the pre-registered MDE, the label-reliability check passes, and the placebo is null. If the sample does not reach the MDE, report the result as inconclusive and do not claim rejection.",
  "data_version": "NBA stats API per-game files for 2022-23, 2023-24, and 2024-25 regular seasons and playoffs, and 2025-26 regular season and playoffs as complete on 2026-08-08 (regular season complete from 2026-04-13; playoffs complete from 2026-06-21). Freeze the data version before analysis."
 }
}

